{#-
  data-form="contact" — email + message required, name and phone optional.

  The export ships this one LIVE, with an inline script that fakes a success
  state. That contradicts the export's own rule that every form is disabled
  until it can really work (README §5, CONTENT.md "never do these" #10), and
  the inline script is blocked by this site's CSP in any case.

  Its own switch (contact form, 2026-10-19; CHG-005): features.contactFormOpen,
  NOT formsOpen, which keeps the pledge and updates sign-ups off. While it is
  off, the forms-off block below renders, exactly as before. While it is on,
  the form posts to the same-origin handler /api/contact
  (website/functions/api/contact.js), which emails the message to the founder
  inbox and stores nothing. With JS on, ui.js sends it with fetch and writes
  the result into .cnote; with JS off, the browser posts it and lands on
  /contact/sent/ (or /contact/not-sent/). Native validation (no novalidate)
  marks and announces a missing or malformed email or a missing message in
  both modes. hp_url is a honeypot, hidden from people and from assistive
  technology and checked on the server.
-#}
{% if features.contactFormOpen %}
<form class="cform" data-form="contact" data-live action="/api/contact" method="post">
  <div class="row2">
    <div><label class="fl" for="c-name">Name</label><input class="field" id="c-name" type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" maxlength="200" placeholder="Your name"></div>
    <div><label class="fl" for="c-email">Email <span class="req">(required)</span></label><input class="field" id="c-email" type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" maxlength="254" placeholder="you@example.com" required></div>
  </div>
  <label class="fl" for="c-phone">Phone</label><input class="field" id="c-phone" type="tel" name="phone" autocomplete="tel" maxlength="40" placeholder="Optional">
  <label class="fl" for="c-msg">Message <span class="req">(required)</span></label><textarea class="field" id="c-msg" name="message" maxlength="5000" placeholder="What&rsquo;s on your mind?" required></textarea>
  <div class="hp" hidden><label for="c-hp">Leave this field empty</label><input id="c-hp" name="hp_url" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></div>
  <p class="cprivacy">We use your details only to reply. Your message goes to our inbox and isn&rsquo;t stored on this site. <a href="/privacy/#s2">Privacy</a></p>
  <button class="cbtn" type="submit">Send message</button>
  <div class="cnote" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></div>
</form>
{% else %}
<div class="form-off" data-contact-form data-form="contact">
  <div class="form-off-msg">Sign-ups open soon.</div>
  <div class="form-off-sub">The contact form opens soon. In the meantime, email works &mdash; the address is just below.</div>
</div>
{% endif %}
